  "source_name": "https://www.whattoexpect.com/pregnancy-weight-gain-calculator",
  "source_type": "website",
  "structure": {
    "block_count": 43,
    "blocks": [
      {
        "block_id": "block_000000",
        "block_index": 0,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h1",
        "text": "Pregnancy Weight Gain Calculator",
        "text_sha256": "e5138ff5c6aad8aaaea4dfa2270782a5da674361763e2800e34ee137de9143c9",
        "word_count": 4
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000001",
        "block_index": 1,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Pregnancy weight gain isn’t one-size-fits-all, but this tool can give you a general idea of what to expect week-by-week.",
        "text_sha256": "a3bfd930ad0d5cf710be1a927d2ef6bcd23694bf9ddf7dd23f924ce055f7c7a0",
        "word_count": 19
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000002",
        "block_index": 2,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Of the many body changes you experience during pregnancy, weight gain is one of the most important. Extra pounds help support your baby’s growth and development from an itty bitty embryo to a newborn ready for life outside the womb.",
        "text_sha256": "6f279399b3fc2699b6df0bfb2531f90c3857a95f76d52f7396ddcfb0d3121d7f",
        "word_count": 40
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000003",
        "block_index": 3,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "In addition to the weight of your baby, the placenta, amniotic fluid, breast tissue and increased blood volume also add crucial pounds to your pregnancy weight. Trusted SourceCenters for Disease Control and PreventionWeight Gain During PregnancySee All Sources [1]",
        "text_sha256": "d5159746b4e24ce18affedf286c78e6b35844155edbb2f6238cb182f8e5cdc65",
        "word_count": 39
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000004",
        "block_index": 4,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Trusted SourceCenters for Disease Control and PreventionWeight Gain During PregnancySee All Sources",
        "text_sha256": "aa95074eec2737f3b20f304ab42b2d2be3457b2cc243edafa2b8fc4d30f719fa",
        "word_count": 12
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000005",
        "block_index": 5,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "If you’re not sure how much you can expect to gain each week and trimester , this pregnancy weight gain calculator tool can help. But keep in mind that there’s a wide range of what’s considered “normal” when it comes to weight gain during pregnancy.",
        "text_sha256": "fd502186ac3f351c055f8f3cef9f15bdb2984a1d0f535d867d16443e565e3de1",
        "word_count": 45
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000006",
        "block_index": 6,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "The total weight you end up gaining will depend on a variety of factors, including your metabolism, activity level, genetics and whether you’re carrying twins or multiples , to name a few.",
        "text_sha256": "e45950bf48db2124df19a7c49ce5d421041fca22411d185d2d848860ccc3bda1",
        "word_count": 32
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000007",
        "block_index": 7,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Remember, this is an educational tool meant to give you a rough idea of how much weight you might gain during your pregnancy, not a substitute for your health care provider’s guidance.",
        "text_sha256": "b7a0db7fa17e8b17a79b05555697b27bc25294abb48c7d18b5815e8725158bf3",
        "word_count": 32
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000008",
        "block_index": 8,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "More important than the number on the scale is keeping up with your prenatal appointments . If you’re worried that you’re gaining too slowly or quickly, bring up your concerns with your doctor or midwife. They can help determine whether you’re on track.",
        "text_sha256": "60ec48e9c4ead5e0736b5f05c558450a2b33da61988cd5fc2ce7a53c9d2b8e4d",
        "word_count": 43
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000009",
        "block_index": 9,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "You can keep track of your weight gain — and any questions you have for your doctor — with My Journal on the What to Expect app.",
        "text_sha256": "118095a16b9ce5c7b6716aaed064a6b1f0570f30bc9500a353c3e2e77daff168",
        "word_count": 27
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000010",
        "block_index": 10,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "How much weight should you gain during pregnancy and what is \"normal\"?",
        "text_sha256": "09dcbc131ae23231fcb5320d9f2fb525ca24ef58249e280da99391be0d693006",
        "word_count": 12
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000011",
        "block_index": 11,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "How much weight should you gain during pregnancy and what is \"normal\"?",
        "text_sha256": "09dcbc131ae23231fcb5320d9f2fb525ca24ef58249e280da99391be0d693006",
        "word_count": 12
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000012",
        "block_index": 12,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Pregnancy weight gain isn’t one-size-fits-all. The recommended weight range a mom-to-be should aim for varies depending on her pre-pregnancy weight, body mass index (BMI) and whether she’s expecting multiples.",
        "text_sha256": "ad829e7c5c06ae2e073524d68dec6abd77d7d6d7841559666e155fceb98debaf",
        "word_count": 29
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000013",
        "block_index": 13,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "The tool above can help you calculate your BMI to determine your suggested pregnancy weight gain. But in general, the American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists (ACOG) recommends Trusted SourceAmerican College of Obstetricians and GynecologistsWeight Gain During PregnancySee All Sources [2] the following:",
        "text_sha256": "8867b983f81f08769581fc8c73de408d366a0d1f03a23139b199534597c8b014",
        "word_count": 43
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000014",
        "block_index": 14,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Trusted SourceAmerican College of Obstetricians and GynecologistsWeight Gain During PregnancySee All Sources",
        "text_sha256": "a13a7ef6261433828eaa24352f426230087f96e7bc389981b9789befba515576",
        "word_count": 12
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000015",
        "block_index": 15,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Pre-pregnancy BMI is less than 18.5: 28 to 40 pounds",
        "text_sha256": "9e8ea9ba059feb212a38b32b4a4b20618f471bc1aa7f87cb7fd5c2e58054009f",
        "word_count": 10
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000016",
        "block_index": 16,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Pre-pregnancy BMI is 18.5 to 24.9: 25 to 35 pounds",
        "text_sha256": "25cd2a7df3a4f4d96c3118122081f10c1cc41a310f01e065e157c1276a4081f2",
        "word_count": 10
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000017",
        "block_index": 17,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Pre-pregnancy BMI is 25 to 29.9: 15 to 25 pounds",
        "text_sha256": "fb5df5a2822863c8f4cd8d5a5ae45570bcc541c9870f6918537d4f10f900dec0",
        "word_count": 10
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000018",
        "block_index": 18,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Pre-pregnancy BMI is 30 or higher: 11 to 20 pounds",
        "text_sha256": "ca76eef842fe1963a50a6d5d8638f37326d752f3aa36edac7c66c02073838a53",
        "word_count": 10
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000019",
        "block_index": 19,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "If you're carrying multiples, the recommended weight gain for twins is as follows:",
        "text_sha256": "dbe05767cdffa52722ab92921dfc8683e489f183275d5722807ccf42ac3c5337",
        "word_count": 13
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000020",
        "block_index": 20,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Pre-pregnancy BMI is less than 18.5: 50 to 62 pounds",
        "text_sha256": "0deba86bdd1c0a21f7557b696551a9c6be4f04ef0bbc3bc46fd0cbbeffc30fd3",
        "word_count": 10
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000021",
        "block_index": 21,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Pre-pregnancy BMI is 18.5 to 24.9: 37 to 54 pounds",
        "text_sha256": "b51b669d82418f44da76030ecd892e332cb6603b76b260b65d02c104b4aa4ddc",
        "word_count": 10
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000022",
        "block_index": 22,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Pre-pregnancy BMI is 25 to 29.9: 31 to 50 pounds",
        "text_sha256": "8d8aeeea79ab6c23ed1b4e799b3e7813d6dd7f04cd0f60ec9e682c130868c9ad",
        "word_count": 10
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000023",
        "block_index": 23,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Pre-pregnancy BMI is 30 or higher: 25 to 42 pounds",
        "text_sha256": "c77023dee1f0298c2e64b3875154c8f08aef05873f2d7f1939f21d5df77e6202",
        "word_count": 10
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000024",
        "block_index": 24,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "See the breakdown in this pregnancy weight gain chart:",
        "text_sha256": "c24a77dace776c39fa20db099cbc6f8083329747448161936b23a8bfc2695052",
        "word_count": 9
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000025",
        "block_index": 25,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "pregnancy weight gain chart",
        "text_sha256": "9c528798aef2be3b730e47b6a0f77658cfec2fe12a3cd9914463a682690e989d",
        "word_count": 4
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000026",
        "block_index": 26,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Using BMI as a gauge for weight gain of any kind has become controversial in recent years, and some experts believe it’s a flawed way of tracking a person’s health.",
        "text_sha256": "ce4497b913cc26225d80f33d44cd6427af11c80754c7755340a968e2c2b05cde",
        "word_count": 30
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000027",
        "block_index": 27,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "However, because ACOG, the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC), and various other medical and health experts still quantify pregnancy weight gain using pre-pregnancy BMI, our pregnancy weight gain calculator incorporates your BMI before pregnancy as a jumping-off point to determine the range for how much weight you may gain while you’re expecting.",
        "text_sha256": "7c92b5c1f2ba610af824c40eb98ebc55cda1d91ad27ae37de94253645ba6cca0",
        "word_count": 54
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000028",
        "block_index": 28,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Just remember that this tool isn’t meant to replace the advice of your health care provider, and there are a host of factors aside from your pre-pregnancy BMI that contribute to how much weight you may gain during pregnancy, as well as your overall health. Always talk to your health care provider if you have any questions or concerns.",
        "text_sha256": "0cfc1b63f1ebe8e2495e78c2274a212c7bbd2902e0f468cc4351113a23dcbbd0",
        "word_count": 59
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000029",
        "block_index": 29,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Pregnancy weight gain by week",
        "text_sha256": "1aa35f92d35b3970a7f24992e878fbc80d153938df779bb6290c98e9084e5a11",
        "word_count": 5
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000030",
        "block_index": 30,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Your week-by-week pregnancy weight gain will vary depending on your metabolism, activity level and genetics. However, ACOG recommends the following weight gain per week for trimesters two and three:",
        "text_sha256": "e5e069b0c0627420db7967347066329b5a02224581bf4c7d2b224c28b29d4089",
        "word_count": 29
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000031",
        "block_index": 31,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Pre-pregnancy BMI is less than 18.5: 1 (1 to 1.3) pounds per week",
        "text_sha256": "581abf7e97a409a0a47834d1374eea0a7f55900104df5d07de077f1e34eb3741",
        "word_count": 13
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000032",
        "block_index": 32,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Pre-pregnancy BMI is 18.5 to 24.9: 1 (0.8 to 1) pounds per week",
        "text_sha256": "d84d3601691dafb7ef9115fce45e1ed07f02de6d30ede1c909c612f817126e00",
        "word_count": 13
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000033",
        "block_index": 33,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Pre-pregnancy BMI is 25 to 29.9: 0.6 (0.5 to 0.7) pounds per week",
        "text_sha256": "7ab90501b529027c63ae369f69aaf859d280d0738975926a3fc2ed9a9620e2cc",
        "word_count": 13
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000034",
        "block_index": 34,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Pre-pregnancy BMI is 30 or higher: 0.5 (0.4 to 0.6) pounds per week",
        "text_sha256": "9e49f2b58437a5210f4d4919af1c938da16c5153a43b4efe894dcf8a2883dceb",
        "word_count": 13
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000035",
        "block_index": 35,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Every mom-to-be is different, and pregnancy weight gain (along with pre-pregnancy weight and BMI) are not an exact science. The most important thing is to keep up with your prenatal appointment schedule, do your best to follow a healthy nutrition and exercise plan as much as possible (with the guidance of your practitioner), and bring up any concerns you have with your OB/GYN or midwife.",
        "text_sha256": "303c8b2b774a076f12e06f4c4050dd9018f759e69df5e472ce794c72eede9bcf",
        "word_count": 65
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000036",
        "block_index": 36,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "What moms say about pregnancy weight gain",
        "text_sha256": "cf20399283e3f348958290dab0e4a1ccda465bf797239dcbe7f96133ff9cc758",
        "word_count": 7
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000037",
        "block_index": 37,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "During pregnancy, it’s normal to worry about your weight gain, especially if it falls outside the recommended guidelines for you. But guess what? You're not alone, and you will get through this, say What to Expect Community moms, who have plenty of tips for how they’ve managed concerns about pregnancy weight.",
        "text_sha256": "0dd380c57755bce6b5f74a16530b662a7a8e8a55c41190f8c6f9281715777f37",
        "word_count": 51
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000038",
        "block_index": 38,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "“Look at pregnancy weight gain as a phase,” suggests What to Expect mom TallLady22. “It’s necessary for your body to support the pregnancy now, and you will get … back into shape later on.”",
        "text_sha256": "d772bc4e80112a4034a879dca7b855ab2cfad4d9808d3a1e3af896e4da35c289",
        "word_count": 34
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000039",
        "block_index": 39,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "“Try not to worry,” What to Expect parent lemondrop889 says. “This is a short time, and you can think about [weight] … when you’re not creating magic and growing a baby.”",
        "text_sha256": "f82c83d5de7df1003f1e37c4f432aa2ea4100bab87add757fc81d2fd0c7a87d3",
        "word_count": 31
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000040",
        "block_index": 40,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "“Your body NEEDS to grow and gain weight to help grow a healthy baby,” says parent Reixry. “It’s exactly what it’s meant to do!”",
        "text_sha256": "e4770946f07583220349668f605f4bdc38ebfe9dda3101f138addd5b37024dbb",
        "word_count": 24
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000041",
        "block_index": 41,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "“I decided not to know my weight gain this time because it stresses me out, so unless the doctor said there was a problem, I just wouldn't know about it,” What to Expect Community member elektron62 says.",
        "text_sha256": "b3a58a7ca07a71d8449db2b8dbed183215c416a872138e02bd3ec4200eb13cb9",
        "word_count": 37
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000042",
        "block_index": 42,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Just remember that weight gain when you’re expecting can vary widely from mom to mom and pregnancy to pregnancy. If you have any concerns about your pregnancy weight, don’t be shy about chatting with your doctor or midwife about it.",
